        "original_id": "2c15123c-3761-55d1-9804-d9d750f69e66",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roy Kinneer Patteson Jr., Ben Sira, Joshua son of Sirach\n- Works: Sirach, Book of Ecclesiasticus, Ben Sira Scroll\n- Places: Masada, Palestine, Jerusalem\n- Topics: Biblical Hebrew, Aramaic, Syriac, Hellenistic Greek, ethical teachings, critical Hebrew text\n\nFacts:\n- Sirach, also called the Wisdom of Sirach, the Book of Ecclesiasticus, or Ben Sira, is a work of ethical teachings written around 200 to 175 BCE.\n- Ben Sira of Jerusalem wrote Sirach and is also identified as Joshua son of Sirach, Jesus son of Sirach, or Yeshua ben Eliezer ben Sira.\n- The Ben Sira Scroll was discovered at Masada in Palestine in 1964.\n- Roy Kinneer Patteson Jr. was an American scholar whose knowledge of Biblical Hebrew, Aramaic, Syriac, and Hellenistic Greek enabled him to analyze the text of the Ben Sira Scroll.\n- Roy Kinneer Patteson Jr.'s research established a critical Hebrew text for portions of Sirach, a first-century B.C. book.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
